{
  "is_sufficient": false,
  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "Normalized pooling cancels absolute recurrence strength: arbitrarily weak positive text similarity can produce a full-scale residual. The signed gate also permits subtracting pooled interests, weakening its proposed interpretation.",
    "Reproducibility and feasibility remain unresolved: TF–IDF settings, recency decay, text preprocessing, checkpoint selection, control matching, and budget allocation are unspecified. Literal prefix-by-prefix similarity aggregation risks cubic sequence-length cost.",
    "Lexical overlap may capture brand, boilerplate, or popularity rather than specific interests. Frequency-bin shuffling alone does not isolate these effects, and repeated validation search is not addressed by paired bootstrap intervals."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Clarify whether confidence-aware pooling would better preserve recurrence evidence and whether simpler pooling deserves priority. This also informs the originality assessment.",
      "query": "What prior sequential recommendation methods combine SASRec with text-similarity-weighted historical item-embedding pooling and zero-initialized gated residuals? How do they prevent normalized pooling from amplifying weak semantic evidence, and distinguish recurrence support from ordinary mean or recency pooling?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Resolve implementation difficulty and establish a reproducible configuration within the shared 43,200 GPU-second budget.",
      "query": "How can causal prefix pooling be implemented efficiently in PyTorch when each historical item's support is its maximum TF–IDF similarity to a distinct prefix item at least three positions away? Compare incremental prefix maxima with naive cubic aggregation, including sparse text preprocessing, padding, zero-support handling, and training–inference parity."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Strengthen mechanism controls and uncertainty reporting without changing the pinned evaluation protocol.",
      "query": "For text-augmented sequential recommendation evaluated on fixed sampled candidates, which retrained controls distinguish semantic recurrence from popularity, brand boilerplate, metadata coverage, and generic pooling? How should repeated validation-based model selection be reported when paired user bootstrap intervals condition on one selected model and fixed training seed?"
    }
  ]
}
